to Sir Paul McCartney.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.847 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.483 line:0%
-Okay.
-What year?

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.652 line:0%
-This year.
-Oh, this year.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:11.457 line:0%
-What was Sir Paul's reaction
to the offer?

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.360 line:0%
-Would you like
to hear the song?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.695 line:0%
-No, what was his reaction
first.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.996 line:0%
-I don't doubt
that you have a song.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.097 line:0%
-Yeah. I want to see --

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.266 line:0%
-How did you get it
to Paul McCartney?

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.634 line:0%
-Well, I'm a giant fan of his,

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.869 line:0%
and I think we've kind of become
kind of friends.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.771 line:0%
It's one-sided.
It's a one-sided friendship.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.373 line:0%
-Right.
-I have his cellphone number.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.975 line:0%
-Now I do want
to hear this song.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.811 line:0%
The one-sided-friendship song
that you threw into his face.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.913 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.581 line:0%
-[ Drumming with hands ]

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:38.418 line:0%
[ As Paul McCartney ]
♪ Am I doing it wrong? ♪

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:41.086 line:0%
♪ Am I doing it wrong? ♪
[ Crowd clapping rhythmically ]

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:43.889 line:0%
♪ Am I doing it wrong? ♪

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.625 line:0%
♪ Am I doing it wrong? ♪

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:49.061 line:0%
♪ Am I doing it wrong? ♪

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:50.529 line:0%
-So you sent that to him?

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.565 line:0%
-I left that on his voicemail.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.733 line:0%
